      "side": 0,
      "message": "I think he meant a feature flag as this is not really a system property.\n\nSuch flags are defined in [init_flags.rs](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/common/src/init_flags.rs;l\u003d172?q\u003dpackages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth%2Fsystem%2Fgd%2Frust%2Fcommon%2Fsrc%2Finit_flags.rs) and they need the associated [ffi](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/shim/src/init_flags.rs;l\u003d1?q\u003dinit_flags.rs\u0026sq\u003d).\nThe can be called with `bluetooth::common::init_flags::\u003cxxx\u003e_is_enabled()`\n\nThe benefit of feature flag as opposed to system property is that they can be change on server side and they will trigger a bluetooth restart to take the new config",
